+// fcSockWait is how long a freshly spawned Firecracker gets to start ACCEPTING
+// on its API socket (RLP_FC_SOCK_WAIT_MS, default 3000). The 3s literal this
+// replaces dates from the original snapshot-resume commit, when a create burst
+// was a handful of VMs; at 1000-wide the spawn storm routinely exceeds it, and
+// the timeout fails the clone -> job redelivery -> retried create, which is
+// also what feeds the consecutive-boot-failure self-cordon breaker. Raising it
+// trades a slower failure verdict for not re-queueing a VM that was merely
+// slow to accept.
+func fcSockWait() time.Duration {
+	return time.Duration(envInt("RLP_FC_SOCK_WAIT_MS", 3000)) * time.Millisecond
+}
